LIGHT = """THE LIGHT AND THE PLAIN: the shortest day of the year on Salisbury Plain, England. A low winter sun in the south-west, sinking through the film: {light}. White frost on the grass in the shadows, long blue shadows, breath-cold clear air, a wide pale sky with thin streaks of cloud, bare trees on the skyline, crows. The sun is always visible or clearly felt: it is the film's clock.
THE TWO TIMES: panels marked PAST are 2500 BC (the new white monument, alien crew, ring ship); panels marked TODAY are the present-day ruin. Spud looks the same in both. A PAST panel that follows a TODAY panel keeps exactly the same framing."""

